Limits on initialization values

When using a literal for initialization, the programmer must ensure that the literal's value falls within the appropriate
	numeric range, e.g., -2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647 for an integer.
	The wrapper classes (except for Character and Boolean) declare the MAX_VALUE and MIN_VALUE fields, which are static fields
	initialized with the maximum and minimum values a type may represent, respectively. A programmer may access these fields to
	check the supported numeric range by typing the wrapper class' name followed by a dot and the field name, as in
	Integer.MIN_VALUE, which returns -2,147,483,648.

